WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.513
Someone sent you a link.

00:00:03.713 --> 00:00:05.673
This is how you join their Popkin.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.387
Open it, and you see what you are joining.

00:00:10.587 --> 00:00:16.165
Mara invited you to Lakeside Weekend: fourteen people, here until Sunday at six.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.064
Before you join, that is all the invite shows: the name, the emoji and colour, how

00:00:23.064 --> 00:00:27.749
many people, up to five avatars, when it wraps up, and who invited you.

00:00:27.949 --> 00:00:31.778
No other names, no messages, no photos of the Popkin.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.345
On a wider screen, a picture of a lake sits beside it.

00:00:35.545 --> 00:00:38.806
It is a stock picture, not a photo from the Popkin.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.103
Choose Join.

00:00:41.303 --> 00:00:45.781
If you are new, you sign up with a six-digit code, and land on the next step without

00:00:45.781 --> 00:00:47.307
opening the link again.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.600
How should people know you?

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.935
Your name is already there, and a photo is optional.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.905
Choose a photo and it takes the place of your initial.

00:00:57.105 --> 00:01:00.794
Without one, you show as initials on a colour that stays yours.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.166
A photo must be one of four common formats, and ten megabytes at most; anything else

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:09.126
is refused, with a message.

00:01:09.326 --> 00:01:14.009
On the server it is checked by its bytes, turned upright, shrunk, and stripped of

00:01:14.009 --> 00:01:15.755
location and device data.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.636
Say I'm in, and you are.

00:01:17.836 --> 00:01:22.748
Welcome in, Joel. You are now a member of Lakeside Weekend, with Mara, Walt and

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:23.919
twelve others.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.234
On a tablet or a desktop, the profile step shows who is already in.

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:33.086
And every screen works in light and in dark.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.011
Not every invite can be joined.

00:01:36.211 --> 00:01:40.885
A Popkin that has wrapped up says so, and offers to start your own. A code that

00:01:40.885 --> 00:01:42.842
matches nothing says so too.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.296
What no screen shows, the tests prove.

00:01:46.496 --> 00:01:51.144
A member who opens the invite goes straight to their Popkin, and guessing codes is

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.768
limited to twenty lookups in ten minutes.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.997
Two choices are left for the owner: where photos are stored once Popkin is deployed,

00:01:58.997 --> 00:02:01.260
and who sends the six-digit code.

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:05.069
Saying hi and seeing the photos arrive with later journeys.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.447
That is journey two. Popkin is a free platform for pop-up communities.
